  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> be vertices of a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math> is the circumcentre of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>, then which of the following is NOT correct about <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "ares is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "perimeter is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "circumradius is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "inradius is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>C</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now slope of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;and slope of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>0</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo></math></p><p>Now we can see&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is perpendicular to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math>.</p><p>So, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is right angled at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>.</p><p>So, Circumcentre <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo></math>mid point of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now given circumcentre&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>So on comparing we get,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math></p><p>Now plotting the diagram and&nbsp;finding the sides with distance formula we get,</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0067_06a9a229c636.png\" style=\"width: 294px; height: 180px;\" /></p><p>Area&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mn>6</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mn>8</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn></math></p><p>Perimeter&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn></math></p><p>Circumradius&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>Inradius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>s</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>24</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
